{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 280,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This video was made possible by Anker – more\non that later."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3520,
    "dDurationMs": 4660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Over the last twenty years, a slew of ever-lighter,\never-more-powerful rechargeable batteries"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 8180,
    "dDurationMs": 4740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has enabled the rise of smartphones, miniature\nhigh definition cameras, drones, commercially"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12920,
    "dDurationMs": 2679,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "competitive electric cars, wireless headphones,\nand so on."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15599,
    "dDurationMs": 3471,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It seems like we’re moving towards a future\nwhere the entire planet is battery-powered,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 19070,
    "dDurationMs": 5180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but there are two big factors that will come\ninto play: 1) how light and energy dense we"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24250,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "can make batteries, and 2) whether we’ll\neven be able to physically manufacture enough"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 29290,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "batteries."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30290,
    "dDurationMs": 3870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This video covers part 1 of this question,\nand Brian of Real Engineering is covering"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34160,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "part 2 – we’ll link to his video at the\nend."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 36760,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ok, so batteries have been getting better\nand better, and nowadays, they can store over"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 40260,
    "dDurationMs": 4599,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "twice as much energy per kilogram as in the\n1990s , which means they’re half the weight"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 44859,
    "dDurationMs": 1581,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for the same energy stored."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46440,
    "dDurationMs": 2239,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hence all the drones and smart phones."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 48679,
    "dDurationMs": 2181,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what’s the limit to this trend?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50860,
    "dDurationMs": 4219,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Batteries are, in principle, fairly simple:\ntake two partially dissolved metals, one whose"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 55079,
    "dDurationMs": 4841,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "atoms want to dissolve more and give up electrons,\nand one whose atoms want to deposit back on"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 59920,
    "dDurationMs": 2930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the solid bit but need spare electrons to\ndo so."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 62850,
    "dDurationMs": 3260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When you put these two together connected\nwith a wire or some other conductor , they’ll"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66110,
    "dDurationMs": 4630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "satisfy each others’ wants, either dissolving\nmore or depositing more, and sending the electrons"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 70740,
    "dDurationMs": 1720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to each other along the wire."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 72460,
    "dDurationMs": 1670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Voilá: electricity!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 74130,
    "dDurationMs": 3510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if you force electricity backwards through\nthe wire they’ll reverse their dissolving"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 77640,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and depositing, otherwise known as “re-charging”."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 80250,
    "dDurationMs": 4479,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The intrinsic limits to how lightweight batteries\ncan be are imposed by two factors: the weight"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 84729,
    "dDurationMs": 4611,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the two materials you use, and how much\nenergy they give off per electron traded."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 89340,
    "dDurationMs": 4419,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you want the lightest materials that produce\nthe most energy per electron."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 93759,
    "dDurationMs": 3930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Metals from the left side of the periodic\ntable, like lithium, sodium and beryllium,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 97689,
    "dDurationMs": 4131,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "really want to lose electrons, while atoms\nfrom the right side like fluorine, oxygen,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 101820,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and sulfur really want electrons."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 104010,
    "dDurationMs": 4180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And atoms close to the top are lighter weight,\nso we can just slap together lithium and fluorine"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 108190,
    "dDurationMs": 2289,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and make a perfect battery, right?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 110479,
    "dDurationMs": 5301,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Unfortunately, no – lithium and fluorine\nare way too reactive – one of the only well-documented"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115780,
    "dDurationMs": 4860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "practical uses of a lithium fluorine reaction\nI could find was incredibly powerful and dangerous"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 120640,
    "dDurationMs": 1229,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rocket fuel."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 121869,
    "dDurationMs": 4271,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In practice, the electrochemistry of batteries\nis incredibly complicated, and requires combining"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 126140,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "metals that work well together chemically,\nelectrically, and controllably at normal temperatures"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 130300,
    "dDurationMs": 5269,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and pressures . For example, oxygen is a gas,\nsulfur is a horrible conductor, and sodium"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 135569,
    "dDurationMs": 3971,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "needs to be molten – challenges to using\nany of them to make batteries."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 139540,
    "dDurationMs": 4660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The current standard for lightweight, rechargeable\nand commercially safe batteries uses lithium"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 144200,
    "dDurationMs": 5019,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and graphite on one side, with a variety of\noptions for the other side, often cobalt oxide"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 149219,
    "dDurationMs": 4432,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": ". Lithium atoms are what either dissolve or\ndeposit in order to transfer electrons, hence"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 153651,
    "dDurationMs": 4039,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the name “lithium ion”, while the other\nmaterials are dead weight along for the ride"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 157690,
    "dDurationMs": 4010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "– I mean, they play important chemical\nroles, but they greatly increase the weight-per-electron"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 161700,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "transferred."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 162700,
    "dDurationMs": 2270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So how much lighter will batteries get?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164970,
    "dDurationMs": 3799,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Theoretical calculations put the minimum possible\nweight for lithium ion batteries at around"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 168769,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "half what they currently are .\nA lighter candidate currently being developed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 172069,
    "dDurationMs": 4411,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is the lithium-sulfur battery , which has\na similar amount energy-per-electron as lithium-ion"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 176480,
    "dDurationMs": 3929,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "batteries, but lithium and sulfur are lighter\nthan lithium and cobalt, oxygen and carbon"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 180409,
    "dDurationMs": 4251,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": ", so a battery with equivalent capacity can\nin principle weigh around a third as much"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 184660,
    "dDurationMs": 2680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": ".\nEven better, lithium-oxygen batteries , while"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 187340,
    "dDurationMs": 4110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "still an incredibly far-off technology, are\ntheoretically four times lighter than lithium"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 191450,
    "dDurationMs": 1210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sulfur batteries."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 192660,
    "dDurationMs": 3370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But that’s pretty close to the limit for\nchemical-reaction-based batteries – there"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 196030,
    "dDurationMs": 3709,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "aren’t really any materials that give off\nmore energy per electron for a given weight"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 199739,
    "dDurationMs": 4451,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than lithium on the dissolving side and fluorine\non the depositing side , and a lithium-fluorine"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 204190,
    "dDurationMs": 4230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "battery – as dangerous and impossible as\nit is – is limited to only be about 10%"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 208420,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "lighter than a lithium-oxygen battery .\nSo the theoretical lower limit for batteries,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 212560,
    "dDurationMs": 2420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "period, is about 5% of current weights."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 214980,
    "dDurationMs": 3950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But that’s an incredible long-shot, everything-works-out,\nperfect world scenario."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 218930,
    "dDurationMs": 4910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "More likely is that we end up combining pretty-good\nbatteries with supercapacitors, fuel cells,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 223840,
    "dDurationMs": 4220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hydropower and other mechanical energy storage\ntypes, and airplanes will probably always"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 228060,
    "dDurationMs": 2539,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have to use some sort of hydrocarbon fuel."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 230599,
    "dDurationMs": 1941,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or maybe we’ll finally figure out fusion."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 232540,
    "dDurationMs": 4459,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ok, so here’s an example of the amazing\nbattery technology we have available today"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 236999,
    "dDurationMs": 3891,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": ": this battery pack is crazy small and light\n– it’s basically eight of these with"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 240890,
    "dDurationMs": 5250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "some clever circuitry – and it has enough\nenergy to charge a smartphone 10 times, which"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 246140,
    "dDurationMs": 7189,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is equivalent to running this LED lightbulb\nfor 10 hours."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 253329,
    "dDurationMs": 3701,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The makers of this ridiculous battery pack,\nAnker, are sponsoring this video and also"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 257030,
    "dDurationMs": 4910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "running a ridiculous contest where they’re\ngiving away ten prizes of two thousand dollars"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 261940,
    "dDurationMs": 3539,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "plus one of their battery packs – they’re\nasking for video submissions about a time"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 265479,
    "dDurationMs": 5091,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that running out of power was awkward or unpleasant\n– you know, like how Apollo 13 almost ran"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 270570,
    "dDurationMs": 4330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "out of batteries, or how I only made it halfway\nthrough mowing the lawn last week."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 274900,
    "dDurationMs": 3930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can find out more about Anker’s batteries\nand the contest by going to the links in the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 278830,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "video description."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 279830,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And one aspect of batteries I haven’t mentioned\nat all yet is power delivery - aka, how quickly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 283150,
    "dDurationMs": 4079,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they can charge your devices – this battery\npack is smart enough to detect what you’ve"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 287229,
    "dDurationMs": 3021,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "got plugged in in order to optimize charging\ntime."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 290250,
    "dDurationMs": 3100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And of course don’t forget to check out\nBrian’s video about whether or not it’s"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 293350,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "even possible to make enough batteries to\npower the planet."
    } ]
  } ]
}
